+# Phase E6 — `keystone-inventory` (v1.11.0)
+
+Driven by the Gangland Warfare 0.9.2 decoupling wave (`brainstorming/decoupling-wave-2026-09-14/`, workstream WS2,
+re-targeted from "Gangland adopts Oriel" to "the basic mechanism moves to Keystone" — R10): the basic inventory
+mechanism both Oriel and Gangland were independently carrying — holder-identified menus, one click/drag/close/quit
+listener, slot click routing, plain components, open/close tracking, panel flows, page arithmetic — is generic
+infrastructure of the same kind as `keystone-command` or `keystone-hologram`, and moves to a new module. Oriel keeps
+the advanced menu product on top (animation, requirements, argument bindings, provider/filter/sort/search
+registries, deposit slots, non-chest menu types, YAML loaders, the editor).
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Version | `1.10.0 → **1.11.0**` (single `${revision}` bump in the root pom; new module is a minor) |
+| Driver | `plans/WS2-inventory-keystone.md`, `docs/extraction-roadmap.md` "Phase E6", plan review `brainstorming/decoupling-wave-2026-09-14/exec/WS2/E6-plan-review.md` (rulings W23), and orchestrator ruling W26 |
+| New module | `keystone-inventory` (37 files: 30 main, 7 test at E6.1; +8 main, +5 test at E6.2 — 43 main, 12 test total) |
+| Gates | E6.1 core (this doc's §1–§2) + 3 fix rounds (§3) → E6.2 flow + pages + docs (§4–§5) |
+
+## 1. Source: Oriel wins, Gangland contributes two pieces
+
+Oriel's `menu-core`/`chest` is the base (holder-identified, `ClickKind`-resolved, already built on Keystone's
+`PlaceholderProvider`/`ChatUtil`/`Guard`/`CooldownService`). Gangland's `gangland-ui/inventory-api` contributes the
+interactive-slot flag (`SlotView.interactive(boolean)`, `ChestMenuBuilder.interactive(int)` — its "draggable" flag),
+the `MultiPanelInventory` in-place-switch-on-matching-size/title optimization (§4), and the extra arithmetic in
+`PageConfig` (§4). Both source stacks were audited 1.16.5-clean: no Adventure or Paper API,
+`Bukkit.createInventory(holder, size, String)` throughout.
+
+## 2. E6.1 — core
+
+`Menu`/`MenuBuilder`/`CloseReason` (`inventory`); `Component`/`RenderContext`/`SlotView`(+`interactive`)/
+`ItemHoldingComponent` (`inventory.component`); `ClickKind`/`ClickHandler`/`ClickContext`/`SlotHandlers`
+(`inventory.click`); `MenuHolder`/`MenuTarget` (`inventory.spi` — `MenuTarget`'s three finer Oriel deposit defaults
+collapse into one `handleDepositClick(InventoryClickEvent)`); `MenuListener` (`inventory.listener` — one class:
+click/drag/close/quit, service-identity filtered); `OpenMenuTracker`/`DefaultOpenMenuTracker`/`NavigationHistory`
+(`inventory.tracking` — instance-scoped, no static tracker); `MenuRegistry`/`InMemoryMenuRegistry`/`MenuOpener`
+(`inventory.registry`); `InventoryService` (`inventory` — `BeanLifecycle`, owns tracker+registry,
+`registerListeners(JavaPlugin)` following the `HologramService.registerProtection` precedent); `ChestMenu`/
+`ChestMenuBuilder` (`inventory.chest` — non-final, protected extension points for Oriel's rebase to subclass
+instead of re-copy); new plain `ItemComponent` plus `FillComponent`/`BorderComponent`/`LineComponent`
+(`inventory.component`); package-private `ChestClickContext`/`ChestRenderContext`/`ChestSlotView`/
+`PassthroughPlaceholders` (`inventory.chest` — co-located with `ChestMenu`, not a `.internal` sub-package, since
+Java package-private access doesn't cross a sub-package boundary and `ChestMenu` needs direct construction access
+to all three on every render/click pass).
+
+## 3. Item-safety guarantees (three fix rounds, all red-first)
+
+E6.1's re-review process found and fixed three item-loss classes before this module shipped a single line to a
+consumer. Each is a standing guarantee `keystone-inventory` now makes that a consumer building on it can rely on:
+
+1. **A genuine user close (Escape, clicking outside) returns held items.** `MenuTarget.returnHeldItemsOnUserClose(Player)`
+   is called by `MenuListener.onClose`'s tracked, non-veto branch; `ChestMenu` overrides it with the same guarded
+   `returnHeldItems(player, CloseReason.USER, true)` every other close path uses. (Fix round 1, finding F1 — the
+   regression of an already-fixed Oriel bug that would otherwise have shipped in the Keystone base.)
+2. **The pickup-vs-close race cannot duplicate an item.** `ChestMenu.returnHeldItems(Player, CloseReason, boolean
+   skipIfSlotEmpty)` — when a click already moved an item out of its physical slot (Bukkit's natural pickup
+   handling) before a close fires, the guard sees the slot is empty and clears the stale held state WITHOUT
+   returning it again. Pinned by `ChestMenuTest.pickupRaceWithPluginDisableDoesNotDupe`. (Fix round 1, finding F2.)
+3. **A vetoed close's held items are never lost, however the timing lands.** A vetoed close (`MenuTarget.vetoesClose`
+   returns `true`) schedules a reopen for next tick; the player may disconnect before that tick runs, or a
+   reload/shutdown may land inside the same window. `InventoryService` records the pending reopen
+   (`recordPendingReopen`/`consumePendingReopen`, an atomic per-player map) the moment the veto fires; whichever of
+   three things happens first — the scheduled reopen task, `MenuListener.onQuit`, or `InventoryService.closeAll`
+   (the reload/shutdown sweep, which now drains this map too, not just the tracker) — consumes the entry and
+   returns the held items exactly once via the same guarded `close(player, reason)`/`returnHeldItemsOnUserClose`
+   paths as everything else. Pinned by `MenuListenerTest.vetoedCloseThenQuitReturnsHeldItemsExactlyOnceAndTheLateReopenTaskDoesNothing`
+   and `InventoryServiceLifecycleTest.onShutdownDrainsAPendingVetoedReopenAndReturnsItsHeldItemsExactlyOnce`. (Fix
+   rounds 2 and 3.)
+
+Two related, deliberately-not-fixed-here items are recorded as docket rows rather than silently left in the code:
+the interactive-flag staleness across renders (fix round 1, N1/N2 — a builder-marked interactive slot now survives
+an untouched render or `rerenderSlot`, and fill decoration never lands in an interactive slot) is fixed, but a
+player-placed item sitting in an interactive slot that is *not* an `ItemHoldingComponent` is still discarded on
+close — recorded as a consumer responsibility (WS2 plan G4), not a Keystone-side gap, since the basic mechanism has
+no way to know a plain interactive slot is holding something worth returning without the marker interface.
+
+Full detail, every red/green line, and the build summary per round: `exec/KS2/E6.1-report.md` ("Fix round 1"/"Fix
+round 2"/"Fix round 3" sections).
+
+## 4. E6.2 — flow + pages
+
+**`MenuFlow`/`MenuFlowBuilder`/`Panel`/`FlowState`** (`inventory.flow`) — reconciled from Oriel's committed
+`chest/flow` (commit `00b8b35`) and Gangland's `MultiPanelInventory`:
+
+- From Oriel: `rerender()` (re-invokes `Panel.render`, row-count-mismatch falls back to a full reopen), same-id
+  `switchTo` == `rerender()`, `back()`/`hasBack()` (ends the flow on an empty back-stack rather than no-op'ing),
+  `suspend()`/`resume()`/`suppressClose()` for an anvil/sign detour, and — the E6.1 re-review's open note — closing
+  the outgoing menu with `CloseReason.NAVIGATION` on a real panel switch, so an `ItemHoldingComponent` a panel is
+  holding returns instead of being silently abandoned along with the discarded `ChestMenu`. Pinned by
+  `MenuFlowTest.switchToADifferentSizedPanelClosesTheOutgoingMenuWithNavigationSoHeldItemsReturn`.
+- From Gangland: switching to a **different** panel whose size AND title both match the currently-open menu's now
+  happens in place (`adoptComponentsFrom`, no close event, no flicker) instead of a full close+reopen — Oriel's
+  original only special-cased the *same* panel id for this optimization. Pinned by
+  `MenuFlowTest.switchToADifferentPanelWithMatchingSizeAndTitleSwitchesInPlace`.
+- One small cleanup over the Oriel source: its `switchInternal(String, boolean)` took a `trackedAlready` parameter
+  never read anywhere in the method body — dropped in the port.
+
+This module is entirely new code with zero prior tests, so there is no pre-existing "red" baseline for the ported
+pieces to show red against — only the two behaviours above are genuinely new logic; the rest is a faithful port of
+Oriel's already-shipped, already-tested design.
+
+**`PageConfig`** (`inventory.page`) — Oriel's `chest/internal/PageConfig` shape
+(`firstRow`/`lastRow`/`firstCol`/`lastCol`/`slotsPerPage`/`pageCount`/`initialPage`, the `forSize`/`defaultInterior`
+factories) kept as-is, plus one new field, `remainingOnLastPage`, folded in from Gangland's
+`inventory/part/PageConfig` — Gangland's own `remainingAmount = itemsCount - (pages - 1) * perPage`, adapted to
+Oriel's field names. Gangland's `finalPage`/`initialPage` fields (an inventory *size* to build per page, under its
+own per-page-separate-inventory `MultiInventory` model) do not port: Keystone's `PagedRegion` pages within ONE
+fixed-size chest menu, never creates a differently-sized inventory per page, and in Gangland's own two call sites
+both fields were always passed the identical value anyway (`MultiInventoryCreation.java:118,131`) — porting a
+field two call sites never actually varied, for a model this module doesn't have, would be dead flexibility.
+
+**`PagedRegion`** (`inventory.page`, new — shaped after Oriel's `chest.component.PaginatedListComponent` but not
+lifted) — a static utility, not a `Component` and not builder-integrated: `PagedRegion.render(builder, config,
+entries, page)` places a page-sized slice of `List<Entry>` (an `ItemStack` + optional `ClickHandler`) into
+`config`'s rectangular region on a `ChestMenuBuilder`. No page-state object, no `initialize(slotsPerPage)`
+registration step, no built-in previous/next button factories — the consumer owns which page is showing and builds
+its own previous/next buttons that call back into whatever re-renders the menu. Oriel's `PaginatedChestMenu`, its
+nav components, and `PaginatedControlPlaceholders` all stay in Oriel.
+
+## 5. Module joins the shade; docs
+
+`keystone-plugin`'s shade list gained `keystone-inventory`. `CLAUDE.md`: module dependency graph gained the module
+(8 sub-packages listed), the testkit-consumer sentence extended, and the layering bullet rewritten from "planned
+for 1.11.0" / "until E6 lands, no inventory code goes into Keystone" to the landed state — the one-sentence
+summary any docket/report can now cite verbatim: **basic inventory mechanism in Keystone, advanced menu features
+in Oriel.** `README.md`'s `## Modules` table and `docs/README.md`'s index both gained a row.
+
+## 6. Tests
+
+Reactor-wide: **1199** tests, 0 failures, 0 errors (`keystone-inventory` **92** at E6.2 gate-close, up from 72
+after E6warning: in the working copy of 'keystone-inventory/src/main/java/org/luckyraven/keystone/inventory/flow/FlowState.java', LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it
.1's three fix rounds: `MenuFlowTest` 9, `PageConfigTest` 8, `PagedRegionTest` 3, unchanged elsewhere).
+`mvn clean install` green. Jar audit (`unzip -l Keystone-1.11.0.jar`): `org/luckyraven/keystone/inventory/`
+present (51 entries); `testkit`/`mockito` absent (0 matches).
